      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Ian Thomson",
      "description": "Central Retail Park, Chapel Park, Kirkcaldy This retail park is the only one in the town and is located off Western Bogily (Chapel) Roundabout and close to access to the A92 trunk road and Chapel Level (A910).\nCurrently, the largest retail park in Fife with twelve units, including an anchor Sainsbury's store (far right of the picture) and two fast food chains:McDonalds and KFC and one restaurant: Pizza Hut. \n\nA new extension of six new units for the retail park will open in late 2008 will see an anchor B&amp;Q store with builder's yard, an Argos store and 360 new car park spaces. Two units, i believe, which include the General George Carpets in the picture will be demolished and re-located in the new development.",
